@ReleaseManager_Bao This fixes a bug where max_retries=None was (incorrectly) treated as 0, causing jobs to be dropped after a single failure; the scheduler now restores the original semantics where None means unbounded retries so affected jobs will continue to be requeued until success or explicit cancellation.  
When normalization from None occurs the scheduler emits a DEBUG-level structured log with event "scheduler.max_retries_normalized" and fields {"queue": <queue_name>, "raw_max_retries": null, "effective_max_retries": "unbounded"} (no job payload), and it only fires on the None→unbounded normalization path.  
No configuration or tuning is required — this is a drop-in bugfix and safe to roll out.
